[{:name "derive-a-sinc-tail-identity-by-differentiating-cosine-over-x"
  :lane :solve-lane
  :level :strategy
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:problem-class
   "Expose a Dirichlet-test tail estimate for `sinc` on a positive finite interval."
   :statement
   "For `0 < a ≤ b`,
    ∫ x in a..b, Real.sinc x =
      Real.cos a / a - Real.cos b / b -
        ∫ x in a..b, Real.cos x / x ^ 2."
   :route
   ["On `uIcc a b`, use positivity of `a` to show every point is nonzero."
    "Differentiate `fun x => Real.cos x / x`; its derivative is `-sin x/x - cos x/x²`."
    "Use `intervalIntegral.integral_eq_sub_of_hasDerivAt` to integrate the derivative."
    "Split the integral into the sine-over-`x` and cosine-over-`x²` terms."
    "Replace `sin x/x` by `Real.sinc x` almost everywhere on the interval, using nonvanishing there."
    "Rearrange the finite-interval identity."]
   :key-api
   ["intervalIntegral.integral_eq_sub_of_hasDerivAt"
    "intervalIntegral.integral_congr_ae"
    "Real.sinc_of_ne_zero"
    "Set.uIcc_of_le"]
   :witness
