 {:name "extend-a-reciprocal-across-finite-punctures-then-apply-Liouville"
  :lane :solve-lane
  :level :strategy
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:problem-class
   "Show that a holomorphic function on the complement of a finite set, blowing up at every puncture and at infinity, cannot omit a complex value."
   :route
   ["Assume a value `w₀` is omitted and form `(f - w₀)⁻¹` off the finite puncture set `F`."
    "Extend the reciprocal by zero at every point of `F`."
    "Use the given blow-up limit to prove the extension is continuous at each puncture."
    "Apply `Complex.analyticAt_of_differentiable_on_punctured_nhds_of_continuousAt` at every puncture; off `F`, transfer differentiability from the reciprocal by eventual equality."
    "Convert the reciprocal's norm tending to zero at infinity into convergence of the extension to zero along `cocompact ℂ`."
    "Apply `Differentiable.eq_const_of_tendsto_cocompact`; the entire extension is identically zero."
    "Choose a point outside the finite set. There the extension is a reciprocal of a nonzero value and hence nonzero, contradicting constancy."]
   :standard-results
   ["Riemann removable singularity theorem" "Liouville's theorem"]
   :key-api
   ["Complex.analyticAt_of_differentiable_on_punctured_nhds_of_continuousAt"
    "continuousAt_iff_punctured_nhds"
    "Filter.EventuallyEq.differentiableAt_iff"
    "Differentiable.eq_const_of_tendsto_cocompact"
    "Finset.isClosed"]
   :witness
   {:declaration "analytic_blowup_surjective"
    :statement-integrity :intact
    :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"]
    :sorryAx false}
   :rule
   "When a holomorphic function blows up at finitely many punctures and infinity, invert an omitted-value translate: zero-fill the reciprocal, remove the singularities, and let Liouville turn decay at infinity into a contradiction."
   :capture-kind :runner-classical-route-and-ground-control-verification}
