 {:name "avoid-all-finite-punctures-with-erase-complement-and-punctured-nhds"
  :lane :arc-lane
  :level :filter-bookkeeping
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:scope
   {:language :lean4
    :problem
    "Near a chosen `z ∈ F`, show a zero-filled function agrees eventually on `𝓝[≠] z` with the original function defined on `Fᶜ`, without inducting over the finite set."}
   :construction
   ["`F.erase z` is finite and therefore closed."
    "Because `z ∉ F.erase z`, the complement `((F.erase z : Finset ℂ) : Set ℂ)ᶜ` is a neighbourhood of `z`."
    "Restrict that neighbourhood to the punctured filter `𝓝[≠] z`."
    "A point in this intersection is neither `z` nor any point of `F.erase z`, hence is outside all of `F`."
    "Use the resulting eventual non-membership to establish eventual equality with the reciprocal and transfer differentiability."]
   :lean-shape
   ["Obtain the neighbourhood with `(F.erase z).isClosed.isOpen_compl.mem_nhds`."
    "Rewrite through `eventually_nhdsWithin_iff`."
    "Discharge membership using `Finset.mem_erase.mpr ⟨hwz, hwF⟩`."
    "Transfer differentiability with `Filter.EventuallyEq.differentiableAt_iff`."]
   :key-api
   ["Finset.isClosed"
    "eventually_nhdsWithin_iff"
    "Finset.mem_erase"
    "Filter.EventuallyEq.differentiableAt_iff"]
   :rule
   "For a finite exceptional set, isolate one puncture by taking the complement of `F.erase z`, then intersect with `𝓝[≠] z`; this excludes the whole finite set at once and avoids induction."
   :boundary
   "The construction handles finite, topologically discrete punctures. It does not generalize unchanged to an exceptional set accumulating at `z`."
   :capture-kind :runner-filter-construction-and-commit-witnessed}
